### 2. Java Map For Loop

Java

import java.util.*;

public class Main {

public static void main(String[] args) {

Map<Integer, String> map = new HashMap<>();

map.put(101, "Rahul");

map.put(102, "Anu");

map.put(103, "Kumar");

for (Map.Entry<Integer, String> entry : map.entrySet()) {

System.out.println(entry.getKey() + " " + entry.getValue());

}

}

}

### Output

101 Rahul

102 Anu

103 Kumar


