### 📌 30-Second Cheat Sheet (Must Remember)

C++

for(auto i : m)

Key -> i.first

Value -> i.second

Java

for(Map.Entry<K,V> entry : map.entrySet())

Key -> entry.getKey()

Value -> entry.getValue()

Python

for key, value in dict.items()

Key -> key

Value -> value

> 💡 Interview Tip: The most commonly asked traversal syntax is `auto i : map` (C++), `Map.Entry` (Java), and `items()` (Python).

A good next step is to practice these loops with a small problem, like printing the highest-quantity product from a map.


